UnitPoolOracle::GetSurroundingObservations
├── when the target is gt or eq to the newest stored observation timestamp
│   ├── when the target eq the newest stored timestamp
│   │   ├── it should set _beforeOrAt to the newest stored observation
│   │   └── it should set _atOrAfter to the newest stored observation
│   └── when the target is gt the newest stored observation timestamp
│       ├── it should set _beforeOrAt to the newest stored observation
│       ├── it should set _atOrAfter timestamp to the target
│       └── it should set _atOrAfter cumulatives to the interpolation between the newest stored cumulatives and the live cumulatives prorated to the target
└── when the target is lt the newest stored observation timestamp
    ├── when the target is lt the oldest reachable observation timestamp
    │   └── it should revert with ObservationOld
    └── when the target is within the populated range
        ├── when the target eq a stored observation timestamp
        │   ├── it should return the matching observation as either _beforeOrAt or _atOrAfter
        │   └── it should pair the matching observation with its adjacent stored neighbor
        └── when the target is strictly between two stored observations
            ├── it should set _beforeOrAt to the previous observation
            └── it should set _atOrAfter to the next observation
